        "original_id": "824665f0-3542-5515-aab1-f521f75b1329",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Marley Shelton, David M. Evans, Ronny Yu, Angus Macfadyen, Mario Yedidia\n- Films: Grand Canyon, The Sandlot, Pleasantville, Never Been Kissed, Sugar & Spice, Valentine, Warriors of Virtue\n- Topics: Film debuts, teen audience films, coming-of-age baseball films, martial arts fantasy films\n\nFacts:\n- Marley Shelton made her film debut in Grand Canyon in 1991.\n- The Sandlot is a 1993 American coming-of-age baseball film co-written and directed by David M. Evans.\n- The Sandlot tells the story of a group of young baseball players during the summer of 1962.\n- Marley Shelton appeared in The Sandlot in 1993 as part of a run of films aimed at teenage audiences.\n- Warriors of Virtue is a 1997 Chinese-American martial arts fantasy film directed by Ronny Yu.\n- Warriors of Virtue stars Angus Macfadyen, Mario Yedidia, and Marley Shelton.\n- Marley Shelton later appeared in Pleasantville in 1998, Never Been Kissed in 1999, and Sugar & Spice and Valentine in 2001 as part of her teen-oriented film roles.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
